{
  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, known for her clairvoyant abilities and as the daughter of one of Europe's longest-reigning monarchs, wed Durek Verrett, a self-proclaimed sixth-generation shaman from California, on Saturday afternoon. Their wedding in Geiranger was unconventional for a royal event, yet spectators gathered along the cloudy streets hoping to see the bride. At 52 years old, Märtha Louise is the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, and ranks fourth in the line of succession to the Norwegian throne. The couple exchanged vows in a traditional Church of Norway ceremony at the four-star Hotel Union, near the scenic Geiranger fjord. Märtha Louise was joined by seven bridesmaids, including Leah and Emma Behn, her teenage daughters from her first marriage to the late Norwegian author Ari Behn, whom she divorced in 2017. Among the 350 guests were her brother Crown Prince Haakon and his wife Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Sweden's Crown Princess Victoria with Prince Daniel, and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien from the Netherlands. Märtha Louise has led an unconventional royal life, having previously claimed clairvoyance and operated a healing school for a decade where she taught angelic communication. In 2022, she announced she would step down from official royal duties to focus on business ventures with Verrett and to clearly separate their work from the Norwegian royal family. Verrett refers to himself on Instagram as a \"servant of God\" and an \"energy activator,\" counting among his clients Goop founder Gwyneth Paltrow, whom he has described as a \"soul sister.\""
}
```

